{
  "dom_id": "step-q153600",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $4\\le x+7.$",
  "worked_solution": "To isolate $x,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *adding* $7,$ which is *subtracting* $7.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & \\le x+7 \\\\ 4-7 & \\le x+7-7 \\\\ -3 & \\le x+0 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the inequality with the variable on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nx\\ge -3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -3.$",
